    "instructions": "Chopped olives (optional)\nTortillas (Fajita size fits in my pan best, but you can fold and roll to fit whatever you need.)\nCheese (Mexican or Sharp Cheddar work best)\nPreheat oven to 375°.\nCook chicken breasts with seasoning and then shred.  They can either be baked or cooked in a skillet.  If you’re in a real hurry you can substitute canned chicken. Reserve a little bit to put on top of the enchiladas when they’re done.\nCombine ¾ enchilada sauce, chilies, soup, mushrooms, and olives (if desired) in a large mixing bowl.\nDip tortilla into the mixture and place into your baking dish (probably an 11x13 pan)\nSpoon rice, beans, and chicken into the tortilla.  Top with sauce mixture.\nRoll tortilla making sure that the “seam” is on the bottom.\nContinue until the pan is full (usually 6-8 enchiladas).  If there is any remaining sauce mixture, pour it over top of the enchiladas.\nTop with remaining enchilada sauce and then sprinkle with cheese.\nPlace the reserved shredded chicken on the very top.\nCover with foil and bake about 25-30 minutes or until cheese is melted and hot.  Remove foil for last 5 minutes.\nServe with refried beans or Spanish rice."
