    "instructions": "These are almost the exact same as regular tacos.  Just a little different, but equally as yummy!\nFollow directions on seasoning packet.  Warm taco shells (if desired) and serve with whatever stuff you want!  EASY!!  You can serve with a side of refried beans (warm them up and sprinkle a little shredded cheese on top and they look fancy!) and/or some Spanish rice.\nServe over Pepperidge Farm frozen patty shells cooked according to directions on box or ice.\nCrispy Ranch Chicken by Fox 13 (Marge Tuckett)\n2 cups rice Krispies\n½ cup grated Parmesan cheese\n1 envelope ranch salad dressing mix\n2 egg whites, beaten\n8 skinless, boneless chicken thighs\n¼ cup melted butter\nCombine rice Krispies, Parmesan cheese and ranch dressing in a large bowl. Stir together.\nDip chicken thighs into beaten egg whites and then coat evenly in cereal mixture.\nArrange Chicken pieces on a well greased baking sheet. Drizzle melted butter over chicken and bake until golden brown for about 25 minutes at 350°. Serve Hot."
