    "instructions": "Cook chicken with seasoning according to package directions.\nAdd in the pepper and onion at the end of the cooking for about 3-5 minutes.\nServe the chicken and peppers in a dish together\nServe with cheese, salsa, guacamole, and/or sour cream for toppings. You can also serve with a side of refried beans.\nGarden Ranch Pizza by Emily Russ (Adapted from Pampered Chef)\nAbout 1b pizza dough (use about 2/3 for the pizza and make the rest into breadsticks)\n½ cup Mayo\n½ package ranch seasoning salad dressing mix (about 2 Tablespoons)\n2-3 Garlic cloves Pressed (more or less as desired)\n1 Chicken Breast, cooked and shredded (seasoned with season salt and garlic salt)\n½ cup bacon (more or less as desired)\n2 cups shredded mozzarella cheese, divided\n1 cup chopped broccoli (more or less as desired)\n½ cup diced red bell pepper (more or less as desired)\n1 medium carrot or 6-8 baby carrots, shredded (more or less as desired)\n½ cup pitted ripe olives, sliced (optional)\n¼ cup grated fresh Parmesan cheese (optional)\nPreheat oven to 425°.\nCook chicken and shred.  (Or you can use canned chicken)\nShape and press dough into baking stone or pizza dish.  (You can roll the dough if needed.)\nCombine mayo, ranch seasoning, and garlic.  Mix well and spread evenly over crust leaving ½ inch around the edge.  Top with ½ the mozzarella cheese (more or less as desired.)\nSprinkle broccoli, bell pepper, carrot, olives, chicken, and bacon over pizza; top with remaining mozzarella cheese.  Grate Parmesan cheese over pizza (optional).\nBake 18-22 minutes or until edges are golden brown.  Remove from oven; let stand 10 minutes.\nThe great thing about this recipe is you can adjust the ingredients to match your taste.  The original recipe didn’t have chicken or bacon in it.  You can add or take away ingredients that you like/dislike!"
