    "instructions": "Ever3 links sweet Italian sausage, removed from casings (can substitute Hot Italian Sausage)\nCroutons (Rachel Ray says to make your own, but I’m not insane enough to think I can do that in under a day, so I just buy them.)\nThis recipe is easiest and fastest if you get everything pretty much ready before hand.  Then all you have to do is throw it in the pot when it’s time.\nPlace a soup pot on the stove top and preheat to medium high.  Brown and crumble the sausage, drain of excess fat then add pepperoni and ham.  Cook for 2 minutes, then add the bell peppers and onions and cook for 2 or 3 minutes more.  Add the tomatoes and chicken stock and bring to a boil.  Stir in the pasta and cook for 8 minutes.\nTop with croutons and serve."
