    "instructions": "Important: DO NOT refrigerate. If air builds up in the bag, let it out. It is normal for the batter to rise and bubble.\nDay 1 – Do nothing (this is the day you receive the batter) go by date on bag.\nDay 6 – Add 1 cup flour, 1 cup sugar, 1 cup milk then mush bag\nPour the contents of the bag into a bowl.\nAdd 1 ½ cups flour, 1 ½ cups sugar, 1 ½ cups milk\nStir together and then take 4 Ziploc bags and measure out 1 cup of the mixture into each bag.\nLabel the bags with the date that you started the bags (Day 1)\nKeep one bag for yourself and give each bag and a copy of the instructions to friends.\nPreheat oven to 325\nTo the remaining batter add:\n3 eggs½ cup oil\n½ cup applesauce½ cup milk\n1 cup sugar2 tsp cinnamon\n1 ½ tsp baking powder½ tsp salt\n2 cups flour1 large or 2 small boxes of vanilla instant pudding\nGrease 2 large loaf pans and mix additional extra cinnamon and sugar to lightly dust the greased pans. Pour batter into loaf pans and sprinkle cinnamon and sugar lightly on top. Bake approximately 1 hour or until toothpick comes out clean. Let cool slightly in pan until the sides of the bread pull away from the pan. Serve warm or cold."
