    "instructions": "Heat sour cream and shortening until shortening melts, but do not boil.  Let cool.\n2 tbsp yeast (or 2 packets)\n1 cup lukewarm water\nDissolve yeast in water let set until frothy.\nIn large mixing bowl, combine sour cream mixture and yeast mixture.  Then add…\n1 cup sugar\n1 tsp baking soda\n1 tsp salt\n2 well beaten eggs\nFinally add\n7 ½ cups flour\nIt should be a fairly sticky dough.  Cover and let set overnight in the fridge.  Shape rolls\nhow you prefer and put on pans.  Let rise on counter for 3 hours.   Bake at 350 for 9 to 12\nminutes, or until golden.\nAlternative to putting in fridge overnight  is to let rise for 3 hours or more covered on\ncounter, then shape rolls and again let them rise for about 3 hours.  Again, Bake at 350\nfor 9 to 12 minutes."
