    "instructions": "I love ginger snaps. But must they snap? I’ve never been a fan of the snapping. If you are getting on the roller coaster ride that is Holiday Cooking, here is a ticket. Add this soft cookie to your list. It is a staple in our home. Not only do these taste amazing, they make your house smell amazing. So if you find yourself in a bind like I did recently: people are coming over and your house looks like a flea market. Throw a batch of these in the oven and the visitors will be distracted from the messes by the mesmerizing smell in the kitchen.\nPreheat oven to 375. Mix shortening, sugar, egg, and molasses. Then add dry ingredients, including spices. Roll into balls, then roll around in a plate of granulated sugar. Bake for 8 minutes."
