    "instructions": "Roll out and bake at 425 for 5 minutes or until lightly browned.\nCut shortening into dry ingredients.  Lightly mix in wet ingredients.  Do not overmix.  Batter should be lumpy.  Pour into greased-and-floured 8x8 pan.  Top with the following:\n4 Tblsp flour\n6 Tblsp sugar\n1/2 tsp cinnamon\n3 Tblsp butter, cut in\nBake at 400 for 25 minutes.\nSticky Chex Mix from Jan LaMar\n6 cups corn chex cereal\n6 cups honey gram cereal\n2, 4, or 6 cups of bugles (if you like them in it) I do 4 cups\n1 cup sugar\n1 cup karo syrup\n1 cube of butter\nMix the cereal and bugles in a big bowl, and on the stove put in the sugar, karo syrup and butter, bring to a boil for 3 to 4 minutes while stirring the whole time, then pour over cereal and stir until everything is mixed real good."
