    "instructions": "About 1b pizza dough (use about 2/3 for the pizza and make the rest into breadsticks) % cup Mayo % package ranch seasoning salad dressing mix (about 2 tablespoons) 2-3 Garlic cloves Pressed (more or less as desired) 1 Chicken Breast, cooked and shredded (seasoned with season salt and garlic salt) cup bacon (more or less as desired) 2 cups shredded mozzarella cheese, divided 1 cup chopped broccoli (more or less desired) % cup diced red bell pepper (more or less as desired) I medium carrot or 6-8 baby carrots, shredded (more or less as desired) cup pitted ripe olives, sliced (optional) % cup grated fresh Parmesan cheese (optional)\nPreheat oven to 425.\nCook chicken and shred. (Or you can use canned chicken) Shape and press dough into baking stone or pizza dish. (You can roll the dough if needed.) Combine mayo, ranch seasoning, and garlic. Mix well and spread evenly over crust leaving ½ inch around the edge. Top with the mozzarella cheese (more or less as desired.) Sprinkle broccoli, bell pepper, carrot, olives, chicken, and bacon oven pizza: top with remaining mozzarella cheese. Grate Parmesan cheese over pizza (optional).\nBake 18-22 minutes or until edges are golden brown. Remove from oven; let stand 10\nminutes.\nGuacamole\nHeidi's. Guacamole\n4 Hass Avocados\n*3 Tbsp lemon juice\n* 8 dashes Tabasco 2 c Red onions finely diced garlic clove, minced 1 tsp Kosher salt Itp black pepper\nmedium tomato, Seed\nPit Avocados add lemon juice & everything add stice through until finely diced ald tomatoes,"
